 poliocephalus (Gray-headed Swamphen)","Ardea coromanda (Eastern Cattle-Egret)","Halcyon smyrnensis (White-throated Kingfisher)"],"lastObserved":"2026-08-01"},"landAround":{"built":80.8,"tree":18.2,"grass":0.4,"crop":0.2,"bare":0.2,"shrub":0.1},"builtInsideOutlinePct":2.5,"fauna2018":["birds","butterflies"],"plants2018":["emergent","free floating"],"weeds2018":"partial"},"history":{"yearBuilt":1904,"src":{"yearBuilt":"empri-2018","surroundings2018":"empri-2018","onMap1945":"soi-57h9-1945","onMap1955":"ams-nd44-13-1955","onMap1975":"soi-57h9-1980","lastSeenWithWater":"jrc-gsw-1-5","rau1986":"rau-1986"},"surroundings2018":"Park, v, settlement & temple","onMap1945":true,"onMap1955":true,"onMap1975":true,"lastSeenWithWater":2021,"rau1986":{"list":"city","status":"disused","nameAsPrinted":"Kempambudhi tank","tankNo":"698","areaHa":14.84,"condition":"The Kempambudhi tank is located towards west of Gavipuram Guttahalli. The tank is ill kept by allowing sullage water from east and fron south. A swinming pool and a park are developed on the southern side and a tree park in the eastern side. A sizeable water sheet is main-~ tained on the northern side. The tank bund is in good condition. There are historical aonuments on the bund and in the surrounding areas, Some encroachments are seen on the northern side","landUse":"Pari & open spaces","recommendation":"The B.W.S.S.B to stop flow of sullage. Water front shou- 1d be developed. The shore areas and the bund ereas to be planted with trees. The committee recomuends for maintainance of water sheet on the northern side and play ground in the southern side","agency":"Forest Dept. Pourisa Dept","zone":"Between Hosur Road and Mysore Road"}},"links":{"wikidata":"Q107639034","src":{"wikidata":"wikidata-2026-09","commonsCategory":"wikidata-2026-09","wikipedia":"wikipedia-en","osm":"osm-2026-09","bbmpLakePage":"bbmp-lms"},"commonsCategory":"Kempambudhi lake","wikipedia":{"en":{"title":"Kempambudhi Lake","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kempambudhi_Lake","summary":"Lakes and tanks in the metropolitan area of Greater Bangalore and the district of Bangalore Urban are reservoirs of varying sizes constructed over a number of centuries by various empires and dynasties for rainwater harvesting. Historically, these reservoirs were primarily either irrigation tanks or for the water supply, with secondary uses such as bathing and washing. The need for creating and sustaining these man-made dammed freshwater reservoirs was created by the absence of a major river nearby coupled with a growing settlement. As Bangalore grew from a small settlement into a city, both of the primary historical uses of the tanks changed. Agricultural land witnessed urbanization and alternate sources of water were provisioned, such as through borewells, piped reservoir water and later river water from further away."}},"osm":["https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/38047206"],"bbmpLakePage":"https://lms.bbmpgov.in/viewlakenew/24","ids":{"atreeFid":"487","empriCode":"BUBNBKkpb_kr1-44","kgisTankId":"1027","waterBodyCensusId":"2/12/002/276600/1302827/001","bbmpLmsId":"24"}},"photos":[{"title":"Kempambudhi lake, Bangalore (2024) 01.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kempambudhi_lake,_Bangalore_(2024)_01.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kempambudhi_lake%2C_Bangalore_%282024%29_01.jpg/960px-Kempambudhi_lake%2C_Bangalore_%282024%29_01.jpg","width":4080,"height":3072,"author":"Gpkp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","credit":"Gpkp / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons","date":"2024-11-22"},{"title":"Kempambudhi lake, Bangalore (2024) 02.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kempambudhi_lake,_Bangalore_(2024)_02.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Kempambudhi_lake%2C_Bangalore_%282024%29_02.jpg/960px-Kempambudhi_lake%2C_Bangalore_%282024%29_02.jpg","width":4080,"height":3072,"author":"Gpkp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","credit":"Gpkp / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wiki